Here is a C++ program that prints a triangle of stars. Each line of the triangle will have an increasing number of stars, following the pattern 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 stars respectively for a 5-line triangle.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

int main() {
    int n = 5; // Number of rows in the triangle
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
        std::cout << std::string(2 * i - 1, '*') << std::endl;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

